1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,681
Brrr! Who has the warmest coat?

2
00:00:02,931 --> 00:00:04,001
Lulu, Dotty,

3
00:00:04,001 --> 00:00:05,642
or the little birds?

4
00:00:05,892 --> 00:00:07,046
Point to it!

5
00:00:09,046 --> 00:00:11,411
Hmm! Let's find out together!

6
00:00:13,261 --> 00:00:16,434
Mama, my fur coat feels chilly today.

7
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:17,415
Brrr!

8
00:00:17,965 --> 00:00:22,189
Let's visit our friends and ask how they stay warm.

9
00:00:22,739 --> 00:00:25,117
Stay close to me, Pip.

10
00:00:25,667 --> 00:00:26,573
Okay, Mama!

11
00:00:26,573 --> 00:00:27,415
But first,

12
00:00:27,415 --> 00:00:29,033
I need something warm!

13
00:00:30,883 --> 00:00:32,171
Mm! Mm mm mm!

14
00:00:32,571 --> 00:00:33,380
Oh, Pip!

15
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:37,425
You wrapped my long scarf round and round and round!

16
00:00:37,975 --> 00:00:39,705
Where is Pip's nose?

17
00:00:39,705 --> 00:00:41,058
Can you see it?

18
00:00:43,058 --> 00:00:44,230
It's under here!

19
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:44,909
Hee hee!

20
00:00:44,909 --> 00:00:46,019
Too much scarf!

21
00:00:47,869 --> 00:00:50,735
Lulu, how do you stay warm in the snow?

22
00:00:51,285 --> 00:00:55,342
I have a fluffy coat that grows all by itself.

23
00:00:55,592 --> 00:00:58,215
What is my coat made of?

24
00:01:00,215 --> 00:01:02,797
Wool! Soft, cosy wool!

25
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:05,839
Can I feel it?

26
00:01:05,839 --> 00:01:07,032
Pat, pat, pat.

27
00:01:07,282 --> 00:01:08,897
Ooh! So squishy!

28
00:01:09,447 --> 00:01:10,327
Pat, pat,

29
00:01:10,327 --> 00:01:11,501
pat with Pip!

30
00:01:11,501 --> 00:01:13,115
Pat your tummy too!

31
00:01:14,915 --> 00:01:17,743
Is my wool thick or thin?

32
00:01:19,743 --> 00:01:23,513
Thick! Thick wool is like a big fluffy blanket.

33
00:01:25,363 --> 00:01:26,739
Quack, quack!

34
00:01:26,739 --> 00:01:28,286
Hello, friends!

35
00:01:28,836 --> 00:01:31,048
Dotty, you don't have wool.

36
00:01:31,298 --> 00:01:33,375
How do you stay warm?

37
00:01:33,925 --> 00:01:36,829
Do I have fur or feathers?

38
00:01:37,079 --> 00:01:39,117
Shout it out!

39
00:01:41,117 --> 00:01:43,799
Feathers! Under my top feathers,

40
00:01:43,799 --> 00:01:45,944
I have soft, fluffy ones.

41
00:01:47,794 --> 00:01:48,328
Look! A tiny fluffy feather.

42
00:01:48,328 --> 00:01:48,621
It's so light.

43
00:01:48,621 --> 00:01:48,794
Whoosh!

44
00:01:49,194 --> 00:01:52,136
What colour is Dotty's fluffy feather?

45
00:01:54,136 --> 00:01:56,059
Yellow! Like the sun!

46
00:01:56,609 --> 00:01:59,648
Fluffy feathers keep me warm!

47
00:02:01,498 --> 00:02:02,598
Tweet, tweet!

48
00:02:02,898 --> 00:02:03,620
Look up!

49
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:05,590
Little birds on the branch!

50
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:08,928
How many birds can you see?

51
00:02:09,178 --> 00:02:11,294
Count with me!

52
00:02:13,494 --> 00:02:15,036
One, two, three!

53
00:02:15,036 --> 00:02:16,821
Three little birds!

54
00:02:18,621 --> 00:02:19,221
Puff!

55
00:02:19,521 --> 00:02:21,732
Whoa! The birds went puff!

56
00:02:21,982 --> 00:02:25,136
Now they look like round, fluffy balls!

57
00:02:25,686 --> 00:02:30,263
Birds puff up their feathers to keep the warm air close.

58
00:02:32,113 --> 00:02:34,978
Let's puff up like a bird!

59
00:02:35,228 --> 00:02:37,940
Big breath in, and puff!

60
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:42,624
Now flap your little wings.

61
00:02:42,874 --> 00:02:45,190
Flap, flap, flap!

62
00:02:48,290 --> 00:02:49,597
Lulu has wool.

63
00:02:49,597 --> 00:02:51,290
Dotty has feathers.

64
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:52,784
Birds puff up.

65
00:02:52,784 --> 00:02:54,174
I only have fur.

66
00:02:54,724 --> 00:02:56,878
Is fur a warm coat too?

67
00:02:58,878 --> 00:02:59,828
Yes, Pip!

68
00:02:59,828 --> 00:03:02,519
Your fur is your very own coat.

69
00:03:02,769 --> 00:03:03,816
In winter,

70
00:03:03,816 --> 00:03:06,555
puppy fur grows thick and cosy.

71
00:03:08,405 --> 00:03:09,135
Pip! Pip!

72
00:03:09,135 --> 00:03:10,535
You forgot your hat,

73
00:03:10,535 --> 00:03:12,421
your scarf and your mittens!

74
00:03:12,971 --> 00:03:14,354
Honey! Thank you!

75
00:03:14,354 --> 00:03:15,529
Fur and a hat.

76
00:03:15,779 --> 00:03:17,298
Double cosy!

77
00:03:19,148 --> 00:03:20,304
Now I'm warm!

78
00:03:20,304 --> 00:03:22,109
What colour is my hat?

79
00:03:24,109 --> 00:03:26,532
Red! And my mittens are yellow!

80
00:03:27,082 --> 00:03:29,046
Rub your paws together.

81
00:03:29,046 --> 00:03:30,330
Rub, rub, rub!

82
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,864
Feel them get warm?

83
00:03:35,964 --> 00:03:38,387
So who has the warmest coat?

84
00:03:38,637 --> 00:03:39,875
Lulu, Dotty,

85
00:03:39,875 --> 00:03:41,195
or the birds?

86
00:03:43,195 --> 00:03:43,899
I know!

87
00:03:43,899 --> 00:03:47,210
The warmest is all of us, snuggled together!

88
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:49,756
Snuggle close, everyone!

89
00:03:49,756 --> 00:03:51,456
Give yourself a big,

90
00:03:51,456 --> 00:03:52,639
warm hug too!

91
00:03:55,739 --> 00:03:58,316
Let's sing the Warm Coat Song!

92
00:03:58,566 --> 00:04:00,835
Do the actions with us!

93
00:04:01,385 --> 00:04:04,295
Little lamb has woolly wool.

94
00:04:04,545 --> 00:04:05,664
Baa, baa!

95
00:04:05,664 --> 00:04:07,250
Pat, pat, pat!

96
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:11,204
Little duck has fluffy feathers.

97
00:04:11,454 --> 00:04:12,838
Quack, quack!

98
00:04:12,838 --> 00:04:14,569
Flap, flap, flap!

99
00:04:15,369 --> 00:04:18,223
Little bird goes puffy puff.

100
00:04:18,473 --> 00:04:19,602
Tweet, tweet!

101
00:04:19,602 --> 00:04:21,013
Puff, puff, puff!

102
00:04:21,813 --> 00:04:24,197
Little puppy has fuzzy fur.

103
00:04:24,447 --> 00:04:25,568
Woof, woof!

104
00:04:25,568 --> 00:04:26,928
Wag, wag, wag!

105
00:04:29,028 --> 00:04:30,830
Warm coat, warm coat,

106
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,182
snug as can be!

107
00:04:32,432 --> 00:04:33,181
A warm,

108
00:04:33,181 --> 00:04:35,278
cosy coat for you and me!

109
00:04:37,578 --> 00:04:38,774
One more time!

110
00:04:38,774 --> 00:04:40,463
Wag and sing with me!

111
00:04:41,063 --> 00:04:42,865
Warm coat, warm coat,

112
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:44,216
snug as can be!

113
00:04:44,466 --> 00:04:45,215
A warm,

114
00:04:45,215 --> 00:04:47,312
cosy coat for you and me!

115
00:04:48,112 --> 00:04:51,980
Share with a friend and subscribe to Honey Bunny Kidz!

116
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,510
Next time,

117
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:57,085
Pip Puppy and Mimi find warm socks for bedtime!

118
00:04:57,685 --> 00:04:59,355
Woof! Stay cosy, friends!

119
00:04:59,355 --> 00:05:01,800
See you next time on Honey Bunny Kidz!

120
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:07,747
Pip is all warm and cosy now!

121
00:05:07,997 --> 00:05:10,881
What do you wear when it's cold?

122
00:05:11,131 --> 00:05:13,150
Shout it out!

123
00:05:15,150 --> 00:05:17,439
Brrr! Now it's getting dark.

124
00:05:17,689 --> 00:05:19,112
Time for bed!

125
00:05:19,662 --> 00:05:23,008
Are you ready for our bedtime story?

126
00:05:23,258 --> 00:05:25,239
Say, yes!

127
00:05:27,239 --> 00:05:31,777
Yay! It's Pip Puppy and Mimi's Warm Socks Bedtime.

128
00:05:32,027 --> 00:05:33,893
Let's watch!

129
00:05:35,143 --> 00:05:36,661
Ooh! Cold toes!

130
00:05:36,661 --> 00:05:37,758
Cold toes!

131
00:05:38,008 --> 00:05:39,489
Hop, hop, hop!

132
00:05:40,039 --> 00:05:42,769
What can I put on my cold toes?

133
00:05:43,019 --> 00:05:44,269
Shout it out!

134
00:05:46,269 --> 00:05:49,423
Socks! Warm, cosy socks!

135
00:05:51,273 --> 00:05:54,216
It's my sleepover at your house, Mimi.

136
00:05:54,466 --> 00:05:57,369
But my toes are too chilly to sleep!

137
00:05:57,919 --> 00:05:59,603
Don't worry, Pip.

138
00:05:59,603 --> 00:06:02,381
I have a basket full of socks!

139
00:06:02,631 --> 00:06:04,169
Meow!

140
00:06:06,019 --> 00:06:07,536
Wow! So many socks!

141
00:06:07,536 --> 00:06:08,846
Which one first?

142
00:06:09,396 --> 00:06:09,856
Pick one, Pip!

143
00:06:09,856 --> 00:06:10,396
Pull, pull, pull!

144
00:06:12,096 --> 00:06:14,692
Ta-da! I'm all ready for bed!

145
00:06:15,092 --> 00:06:16,118
Hee hee!

146
00:06:16,118 --> 00:06:18,169
A sock on your ear?

147
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:21,342
Does a sock go on your ear?

148
00:06:23,342 --> 00:06:25,631
No! Socks go on your feet!

149
00:06:25,881 --> 00:06:27,054
Silly me!

150
00:06:28,904 --> 00:06:32,096
Let's play a sock colour game!

151
00:06:32,646 --> 00:06:35,358
What colour is this sock?

152
00:06:37,358 --> 00:06:39,742
Red! With little white hearts!

153
00:06:41,592 --> 00:06:42,585
And this one?

154
00:06:42,585 --> 00:06:43,515
What colour?

155
00:06:45,515 --> 00:06:47,711
Yellow! With orange dots,

156
00:06:47,711 --> 00:06:49,515
like little oranges!

157
00:06:51,365 --> 00:06:52,806
Stripy, stripy!

158
00:06:52,806 --> 00:06:56,327
What colour are the stripes on this sock?

159
00:06:58,327 --> 00:06:59,539
Green and white!

160
00:06:59,539 --> 00:07:00,942
Like a candy stick!

161
00:07:03,592 --> 00:07:05,036
Ooh, my favourite!

162
00:07:05,036 --> 00:07:06,823
Blue with yellow stars!

163
00:07:07,073 --> 00:07:09,265
Count the stars with me!

164
00:07:11,065 --> 00:07:13,546
One, two, three stars!

165
00:07:15,346 --> 00:07:17,263
Socks come in twos.

166
00:07:17,263 --> 00:07:19,442
Two socks make a pair!

167
00:07:19,992 --> 00:07:21,496
Red and red.

168
00:07:21,496 --> 00:07:23,300
Is that a pair?

169
00:07:23,550 --> 00:07:25,665
Yes or no?

170
00:07:27,665 --> 00:07:29,278
Yes! Two red socks!

171
00:07:29,278 --> 00:07:30,011
A pair!

172
00:07:31,861 --> 00:07:33,096
Yellow and green.

173
00:07:33,096 --> 00:07:34,207
Is that a pair?

174
00:07:36,207 --> 00:07:38,314
No! They don't match.

175
00:07:38,314 --> 00:07:39,630
Silly socks!

176
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,134
Now we have pairs!

177
00:07:43,134 --> 00:07:45,653
How many pairs can you count?

178
00:07:47,853 --> 00:07:50,757
One, two, three pairs!

179
00:07:51,257 --> 00:07:54,180
Look, I put on one blue star sock.

180
00:07:54,430 --> 00:07:57,046
But where is the other blue sock?

181
00:08:00,346 --> 00:08:02,115
Is it under the rug?

182
00:08:02,115 --> 00:08:02,576
No.

183
00:08:04,626 --> 00:08:08,184
Listen! What is that jingle in my bed?

184
00:08:11,284 --> 00:08:12,491
My blue sock!

185
00:08:12,491 --> 00:08:14,150
It's in Mimi's bed!

186
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:15,156
Oh!

187
00:08:15,156 --> 00:08:19,796
My yarn ball was snuggled inside it like a little blanket!

188
00:08:20,046 --> 00:08:21,699
Hee hee!

189
00:08:23,549 --> 00:08:25,033
One sock, two socks!

190
00:08:25,033 --> 00:08:26,838
Wiggle your toes with me!

191
00:08:28,638 --> 00:08:31,561
Ahh! My toes are warm and cosy now!

192
00:08:32,111 --> 00:08:34,034
Mine too!

193
00:08:35,884 --> 00:08:39,355
Who wants a warm milk cuddle before bed?

194
00:08:39,905 --> 00:08:40,573
Me! Me!

195
00:08:40,573 --> 00:08:41,376
Pad, pad,

196
00:08:41,376 --> 00:08:42,713
pad in our socks!

197
00:08:43,263 --> 00:08:46,102
I made it just warm, not hot.

198
00:08:46,352 --> 00:08:48,415
Stay close to me.

199
00:08:48,965 --> 00:08:51,611
How many cups are on the table?

200
00:08:53,611 --> 00:08:55,392
Two! One for Pip,

201
00:08:55,392 --> 00:08:56,996
and one for me!

202
00:08:58,846 --> 00:09:01,519
Mmm! What do we say to Mama Bunny?

203
00:09:03,519 --> 00:09:04,923
Thank you!

204
00:09:04,923 --> 00:09:05,788
Meow!

205
00:09:06,338 --> 00:09:08,504
Now a big, cosy cuddle.

206
00:09:08,504 --> 00:09:09,670
Look, soft,

207
00:09:09,670 --> 00:09:12,503
sleepy snow is falling outside.

208
00:09:14,353 --> 00:09:17,488
Time for a sleepy kitten stretch!

209
00:09:17,738 --> 00:09:20,507
Paws up high, high, high!

210
00:09:22,507 --> 00:09:24,949
Now wiggle your warm toes.

211
00:09:25,199 --> 00:09:26,603
Wiggle, wiggle!

212
00:09:29,503 --> 00:09:31,142
Now slow breaths.

213
00:09:31,142 --> 00:09:32,290
Breathe in,

214
00:09:32,290 --> 00:09:34,503
like smelling warm milk.

215
00:09:36,503 --> 00:09:37,843
And breathe out,

216
00:09:37,843 --> 00:09:39,041
slow and soft.

217
00:09:39,291 --> 00:09:40,099
Ahh.

218
00:09:43,599 --> 00:09:44,466
Yes, Moon!

219
00:09:44,466 --> 00:09:46,734
Let's sing the Warm Socks Song!

220
00:09:46,984 --> 00:09:48,387
Wiggle along!

221
00:09:50,237 --> 00:09:51,983
One sock, two socks,

222
00:09:51,983 --> 00:09:53,045
on my feet.

223
00:09:53,295 --> 00:09:54,690
Wiggle, wiggle,

224
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:56,007
toes so sweet!

225
00:09:56,607 --> 00:09:58,878
Red socks, blue socks,

226
00:09:58,878 --> 00:10:00,241
find a pair.

227
00:10:00,491 --> 00:10:03,530
Warm and cosy everywhere!

228
00:10:05,430 --> 00:10:07,418
Warm socks, cosy socks,

229
00:10:07,418 --> 00:10:08,795
snug and tight.

230
00:10:09,045 --> 00:10:11,699
Warm socks help me sleep tonight!

231
00:10:13,799 --> 00:10:15,787
Warm socks, cosy socks,

232
00:10:15,787 --> 00:10:17,164
snug and tight.

233
00:10:17,414 --> 00:10:20,068
Warm socks help me sleep tonight!

234
00:10:20,868 --> 00:10:23,580
Yawn! Goodnight, Pip.

235
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:25,356
Goodnight, Mimi.

236
00:10:25,356 --> 00:10:27,095
Goodnight, warm toes.

237
00:10:28,995 --> 00:10:32,990
Wiggle your toes and say goodnight with me.

238
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:34,784
Goodnight!

239
00:10:36,384 --> 00:10:40,252
Share with a friend and subscribe to Honey Bunny Kidz!

240
00:10:40,852 --> 00:10:41,695
Next time,

241
00:10:41,695 --> 00:10:45,781
Pip Puppy counts five little snowflakes in a brand new song!

242
00:10:46,381 --> 00:10:48,303
Sweet dreams, friends!

243
00:10:48,303 --> 00:10:51,455
See you next time on Honey Bunny Kidz!

244
00:10:54,055 --> 00:10:56,342
That's all for now, friends!

245
00:10:56,592 --> 00:10:58,771
Come back soon for more stories

246
00:10:58,771 --> 00:11:00,885
and songs on Honey Bunny Kidz.

247
00:11:01,135 --> 00:11:02,833
Bye bye!
